<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03UW">Remark <span data-tag="03UW">5.5.3.14</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \leq \lambda $ be regular cardinals, where $\lambda $ has exponential cofinality $\geq \kappa $ (Definition <a data-tag="03RT" href="/tag/03RT">4.9.3.16</a>). Then the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ is locally $\lambda $-small. This follows by combining Remarks <a data-tag="020F" href="/tag/020F">5.5.3.5</a> and <a data-tag="03ST" href="/tag/03ST">4.9.5.13</a>. It follows that the full subcategory $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \kappa } \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ is also locally $\lambda $-small. If $\kappa &lt; \lambda $, then $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ are essentially $\lambda $-small (Remark <a data-tag="0614" href="/tag/0614">4.9.4.22</a>). </p>
